  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "A landlord of a rental unit shall pay interest to the tenant annually on the amount of the rent deposit at a rate equal to the guideline determined under section 120 that is in effect at the time payment becomes due.",
  "reason": "Section 106(6) requires the landlord to pay interest annually on the rent deposit. Because this clause waives interest on the rent deposit, it is inconsistent with the Act and is therefore void under section 4(1)."
}

